Z||000000||penetrator||02-10-2000||11:50 AM||||Can a bad battery make your car to stall?<BR>My car used to stall after a couple of minutes driving. And i also discovered that one cell in my battery was really bad and didnt give any power at all.(i didnt check the battery because of the stalling problem=) <BR>But when i installed a new battery, the car spins like a cat, and it started just with a touch on the ignintion. But i now wonder if that also could have caused my stalling ?<P>Thanks<BR>Magnus||||reg||5
Z||000001||lennyb4||02-10-2000||01:20 PM||||I've never heard of a dead / bad battery causing a car to stall unless your alt. is also bad. Your alt. supplies the car with enough power to ensure it will run once started even if you take the battery out. I would take your car to a auto parts store and have them test your charging system while the cars running.||||reg||1
